    {
      "title": "Namespaces and Name Lookup",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Namespaces and Name Lookup",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Namespace Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==namespace== groups names to avoid collisions",
                "`namespace app { int x; }` is used as `app::x`",
                "Can be ==reopened== across files and extended"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. using, Aliases, Headers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Declaration",
                "Directive"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Syntax",
                  "`using std::cout;`",
                  "`using namespace std;`"
                ],
                [
                  "Imports",
                  "one name",
                  "{red:every name}"
                ],
                [
                  "Risk",
                  "low",
                  "ambiguity"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`using namespace` in a header leaks into every includer",
                "Limit it to ==function scope== or .cpp files"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "namespace fs = std::filesystem;",
                "namespace a::b::c { int v; }"
              ],
              "note": "alias shortens names; nested form is C++17"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Argument-Dependent Lookup",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unqualified `swap(a, b)` also searches the ==namespaces of the argument types==",
                "This is why `operator<<` for your own type works"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "namespace geo { struct P { int x; };",
                "                void swap(P&, P&); }",
                "geo::P p, q;",
                "swap(p, q);  // ADL finds geo::swap"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "ADL only applies to **unqualified** calls. Prefer `using std::cout;` over `using namespace std;`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anonymous Namespaces and Internal Linkage",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Anonymous Namespaces and Internal Linkage",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`namespace { int counter = 0; }` gives ==internal linkage==",
                "Members are visible only in {green:that translation unit}",
                "Replaces file-scope `static` on variables and functions",
                "`static` is still needed for {blue:class members} and function-local statics"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why No ODR Clash",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each .cpp gets its own ==unique unnamed namespace==",
                "Same name in two files: {green:no clash}, separate entities",
                "Used {blue:unqualified} in the same file"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "// a.cpp",
                "namespace { int counter = 0; }",
                "// b.cpp",
                "namespace { int counter = 0; }"
              ],
              "note": "two separate counters, links fine"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where to Use It",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "File-local helpers, constants",
                  "`namespace { }` in the .cpp"
                ],
                [
                  "Shared across files",
                  "Named namespace + header declaration"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never in a header",
              "text": "Each includer gets its own ==private copy==: silent duplicates, **not** shared state."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "enum vs enum class",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "enum vs enum class",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Unscoped vs scoped",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "enum",
                "enum class"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Names",
                  "leak into scope",
                  "need `Color::Red`"
                ],
                [
                  "Two `Red`s",
                  "{red:collide}",
                  "{green:no clash}"
                ],
                [
                  "To int",
                  "implicit",
                  "explicit cast only"
                ],
                [
                  "Vs other enum",
                  "comparable",
                  "not comparable"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Casts and underlying type",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`static_cast<int>(Color::Red)` gets the value",
                "`static_cast<Color>(1)` goes back; ==no range check==",
                "Underlying type sets the ==size==",
                "Known underlying type allows ==forward declaration==",
                "A plain enum can too, if its type is fixed: `enum Old : int;`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "enum class Status : uint8_t;  // header",
                "enum class Status : uint8_t { Ok, Fail };",
                "int v = static_cast<int>(Status::Fail);"
              ],
              "note": "declaration matches definition"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which to use",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default: ==enum class==",
                "Plain enum only when you need implicit `int`",
                "Bit flags with enum class need overloaded `|`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Match the type",
              "text": "Bare `enum class Status;` means `int`. If the definition says `: uint8_t`, repeat it."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why prefer enum class?** No leaking, no silent int conversion.",
                "**Why can `enum class Status;` be forward declared?** Its underlying type is known (default int).",
                "**Does `static_cast<Color>(1)` check range?** No."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading and Writing Files with fstream",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Reading and Writing Files with fstream",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Streams and Reading",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Include `<fstream>`: ==ifstream== reads, ==ofstream== writes, ==fstream== does both",
                "File closes when the object leaves scope (**RAII**)",
                "A failed open does {red:not throw}: test `if (!in)`",
                "Lines: `while (std::getline(in, line))`; tokens: `while (in >> x)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::ifstream in(\"a.txt\");",
                "if (!in) { return 1; }",
                "std::string line;",
                "while (std::getline(in, line)) {",
                "    // use line",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "the read is the loop condition"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Writing and Modes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::ofstream out(p, std::ios::app);",
                "out << text << '\\n';"
              ],
              "note": "without ios::app the default truncates"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ios::in` / `ios::out`",
                  "read / write"
                ],
                [
                  "`ios::trunc`",
                  "empty the file on open"
                ],
                [
                  "`ios::app`",
                  "append at the end"
                ],
                [
                  "`ios::binary`",
                  "raw bytes: `read`/`write` take `char*` + size"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Combine flags with `|`: `ios::in | ios::binary`",
                "Prefer `'\\n'`; `std::endl` flushes every time"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`while (!in.eof())` can run one extra time",
                "Skipping the open check",
                "`std::endl` in hot loops"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Put the ==read in the loop condition==, and check the open yourself: nothing throws."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "std::filesystem Paths and Directory Iteration",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "std::filesystem Paths and Directory Iteration",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Paths and Their Parts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`#include <filesystem>` (C++17), then `namespace fs = std::filesystem;`",
                "Old GCC: link with ==-lstdc++fs==",
                "`/` appends: `fs::path p = dir / \"data\" / \"a.txt\"`",
                "Part functions only {blue:manipulate text}; they never touch the disk"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call on data/a.txt",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`p.filename()`",
                  "a.txt"
                ],
                [
                  "`p.stem()`",
                  "a (no extension)"
                ],
                [
                  "`p.extension()`",
                  "==.txt== (dot included)"
                ],
                [
                  "`p.parent_path()`",
                  "data"
                ],
                [
                  "`p.replace_extension(\".csv\")`",
                  "data/a.csv"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Disk Queries",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`exists(p)`",
                  "path exists"
                ],
                [
                  "`is_regular_file(p)` / `is_directory(p)`",
                  "type check"
                ],
                [
                  "`file_size(p)`",
                  "size in bytes"
                ],
                [
                  "`create_directories(p)`",
                  "makes every missing level"
                ],
                [
                  "`remove(p)`",
                  "file or {red:empty} directory only"
                ],
                [
                  "`remove_all(p)`",
                  "deletes ==recursively=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 5
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Iteration and Errors",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::error_code ec;",
                "int dirs = 0;",
                "for (const auto& e :",
                "     fs::recursive_directory_iterator(dir, ec))",
                "    if (e.is_directory()) ++dirs;"
              ],
              "note": "directory_iterator(dir) = one level only"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each entry: `e.path()`, `e.is_directory()`",
                "Iteration order is ==unspecified==",
                "Failure throws `fs::filesystem_error`; a range-for `++` can throw even after passing `ec`",
                "Pass `std::error_code` last for no-throw: `fs::exists(p, ec)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Absolute right side wins",
              "text": "`fs::path(\"data\") / \"/abs\"` is `\"/abs\"`, not data/abs. It replaces the whole path, so never append untrusted components."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Namespaces, Enums, Files",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Namespaces, Enums, Files",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Namespaces and File-Local Names",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Want",
                "Write"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Qualified name",
                  "`ns::name`"
                ],
                [
                  "Import one name",
                  "`using ns::name;`"
                ],
                [
                  "Alias",
                  "`namespace x = ns::deep::path;`"
                ],
                [
                  "File-local helper",
                  "`namespace { ... }` not `static`"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Never}",
                  "`using namespace` in a header"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. enum class",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`enum class E : uint8_t { A, B };` sets the size",
                "Use `E::A`; no implicit int conversion",
                "Convert: `static_cast<int>(e)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. fstream",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::ifstream f(\"a.txt\");",
                "if (!f) return 1;",
                "std::string s;",
                "while (std::getline(f, s)) {}",
                "std::ofstream o(\"b\", std::ios::app);"
              ],
              "note": "ios::binary for raw bytes; combine with |"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. filesystem",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`fs::path p = d / \"x\"`",
                  "append"
                ],
                [
                  "`stem()` / `extension()`",
                  "name / `.ext`"
                ],
                [
                  "`exists(p)`, `create_directories(p)`",
                  "query / create"
                ],
                [
                  "`directory_iterator`, `recursive_directory_iterator`",
                  "one level / deep"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No throw",
              "text": "Pass an ==error_code== last, like `fs::exists(p, ec)`, to avoid `filesystem_error`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: `enum class Color { Red, Green }; int x = Color::Green;`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It fails to compile: enum class has ==no implicit conversion== to int",
                "Fix: `static_cast<int>(Color::Green)`, which gives 1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A file ends with a newline. What goes wrong here?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`eof()` turns true only after a read hits end of file, so the loop runs ==one extra time== on an empty line",
                "Fix: put the read in the condition, `while (std::getline(in, line))`"
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "while (!in.eof()) {",
                "    std::getline(in, line);",
                "    use(line);",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What does this print?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It prints `\"/abs/a.txt\"` ==with the double quotes==, because `operator<<` on fs::path uses std::quoted",
                "Use `p.string()` for unquoted text"
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "fs::path p = \"/abs/a.txt\";",
                "std::cout << p << '\\n';"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
